    "description": "\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tChainSWE\n\t\n\nChainSWE is a benchmark of sequential bug-fix tasks for evaluating coding agents on continuous software maintenance. Each row is one time-ordered sequence in one repository, with a shared base commit and Docker image; bug_fixes contains its ordered tasks.\nThe length-specific splits contain 376 sequences and 1504 bug-fixes.\n\n\t\n\t\t\nSplit\nSequences\nBug-fix occurrences\n\n\n\t\t\nlen_3\n142\n426\n\n\nlen_4\n92\n368\n\n\nlen_5\n142\n710\n\n\nunique\n213\n956\n\n\n\t\n\nunique is a non-overlapping\u2026 See the full description on the dataset page: https://huggingface.co/datasets/C-lister/ChainSWE."
